# Deadly Precision's other additional cost: sacrifice an artifact or creature (CR 601.2b, 118.8). Bot1 has just a Swamp, so the
# spell costs {B} and the Ornithopter is sacrificed instead of paying {4}; its own Island stays in hand. "Destroy target
# creature": Bot2 controls a Mox Emerald (an artifact, not a creature) beside its Llanowar Elves, and the cast aimed at the
# Mox is refused (the positive control is the cast at the Elves on the next line). Only the Elves is destroyed.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Ornithopter
Deadly Precision
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Forest x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Deadly Precision.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald)
Bot1.Hand.Deadly Precision.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Modes(Sacrifice an artifact or creature)
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp
Bot1.Graveyard = Deadly Precision; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Emerald
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
